Let's assume that all options are visible without the need of scrolling, because scrolling would make it much more difficult.
There's a function called Window_Selectable.prototype.itemRect that you can modify for your window to move all options downwards by Y pixels, e.g.
Code:
Custom_Window.prototype.itemRect = function(index) {
  const rect = Window_Selectable.prototype.itemRect.call(this, index);
  rect.y += 100;
  return rect;
}
Or you write any custom function you need for your window.
Then you can draw any additional text like this:
Code:
Custom_Window.prototype.drawAllItems = function() {
  Window_Selectable.prototype.drawAllItems();

  this.drawText("whatever", 0, 0, this.contentsWidth());
}

