I don't really agree with this.  It's great that there is documentation for MZ, but it still isn't very good.  I came to RPG Maker because I was feeling nostalgic and decided on MV because it already had a large amount of available plugins, both free and paid.  Yes, learning how to program can be frustrating but comparing RM to Unity, if I want to do something in Unity, I can just look it up:
Unity - Scripting API: Rigidbody
docs.unity3d.com
All properties, functions, parameters, etc, are all here.  Is it going to be challenging?  Sure, but it's significantly 1000% less challenging and frustrating than having to open up rpg_windows.js and sift through 6000 lines of someone else's code to try and make sense of how these objects work.
This isn't a case of "this is just how it is," I would consider RPG Maker to be up there with the top dogs in terms of availability and popularity.  Godot, Unity, and UE all have clear documentation where RM does not.
